# Two replies are held for a closed session: one because the session was closed when
# it arrived, one because its thread had been waking the session too often. Accepting
# the first from the inbox opens the session and delivers it, once the session has
# drawn. Opening the session must not release the second: it is still a runaway
# thread, and only the user decides on it.

size 110x30
arg --mux
session existing-app Existing app session
held_reply https://github.com/o/r/issues/12
held_reply https://github.com/o/r/issues/13 throttled

wait_for Existing app session
press ctrl+b g m
wait_for issues/12
expect issues/13
dump 01-inbox-with-both

press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
# The inbox stays open over the session while anything is left in it, so the
# throttled reply is still listed there and nowhere else.
wait_gone its session is closed
expect this thread has woken it repeatedly
dump 02-accepted-inbox-still-open

press esc
wait_gone Waiting for you
wait_for Fake Copilot received: A new comment arrived on https://github.com/o/r/issues/12
wait 3000
expect_not issues/13
dump 03-accepted-and-woken

# The stub has no hooks; an Enter stands in for the turn that takes the pointer.
press enter
wait 1500
press ctrl+b d
wait_gone Fake Copilot is idling
press ctrl+b g m
wait_for issues/13
expect_not issues/12
dump 04-inbox-keeps-the-throttled-one
